# Maintainer: Jan Alexander Steffens (heftig) <heftig@archlinux.org>
# Contributor: Eric Bélanger <eric@archlinux.org>
#
# Arch's webkit2gtk-4.1 recipe, with ppc64le added and the JavaScriptCore JIT
# port staged in prepare(). See prepare() and the powerpc64le branches of
# build() for what differs from upstream's.
#
# PORT=GTK BUILDS AND THE RESULT CARRIES THE JIT, measured 2026-10-10 on
# POWER9 with this recipe's own prepare() and build(), CARCH=powerpc64le and
# /etc/makepkg.conf's flags (-mcpu=power9 -mtune=power9):
#
#   926 of 926 ninja edges, zero errors.  libjavascriptcoregtk-4.1.so (51 MB)
#   and libwebkit2gtk-4.1.so (171 MB) link.  The JavaScriptCore library holds
#   1661 PPC64Assembler symbols and 559 MacroAssemblerPPC64, and ZERO CLoop
#   symbols -- so the native LLInt is in, not the portable interpreter.  FTL
#   and the wasm JITs are in too, evidenced by B3::WasmBoundsCheckValue and
#   B3::Procedure::setWasmBoundsCheckGenerator being exported over
#   PPC64Registers::RegisterID.  The jsc shell this build produces, run against
#   that shared library, reports useJIT/useDFGJIT/useFTLJIT/useBBQJIT/useOMGJIT
#   all true and measurably compiles through all three JS tiers: Baseline
#   0.549 ms, DFG 1.175 ms, FTL 2.322 ms.
#
# Packaging is proven now too: webkit2gtk-4.1 2.54.1-1 built, packaged and
# installed on this machine (pacman -U, 2026-10-10), and so did the 6.0
# sibling.  Epiphany 50.4 then ran ten minutes on 6.0 with the JIT live.
#
# That run also found the bug pkgrel 2 exists for.  A code object whose
# baseline machine code exceeds the +-32 MB a `b` reaches used to abort in the
# jump-island allocator: JIT::privateCompileLinkPass() links jumps while the
# code is still in the assembler buffer, and an island has to sit next to the
# branch's FINAL address in the executable pool, which does not exist yet.  One
# ordinary page with a large enough script body was enough -- measured at
# 5,578,642 label slots and ~38 MB of code.  Fixed in the port layer; see
# ppc64le-port/newfiles PPC64Assembler.h linkJump() and the invariant
# tools/edits.py now asserts in ExecutableAllocator.cpp.
#
# The installed base/webkit2gtk-4.1 is 2.50.4 and is a CLoop build with no
# ppc64 JIT symbols at all, so this is also a version bump. ours/artcraft
# depends on webkit2gtk-4.1 and is the consumer that wants the JIT.
#
# This build found one port bug that no PORT=JSCOnly build could: 
# PPC64Assembler.h reached SIMDInfo.h in quotes, which only resolves while
# jit/ is an include directory -- true inside JavaScriptCore, false for
# WebCore, which sees only the forwarding headers.  Fixed in the port
# (21ef9d08f2); it had blocked GTK, WPE and every embedder of them.

